---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Pinto Injury Resources';
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for Pinto Injury Resources. Learn what information we collect, how we use it, and your choices.';
const lastUpdated = 'January 21, 2026';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Header />

    <main class="container" style="padding: 3rem 1rem;">
      <article class="surface" style="max-width: 80ch; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem;">
        <header>
          <h1 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.15;">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p style="margin: 0; opacity: 0.85;">
            <strong>Last updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}
          </p>
        </header>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
          <p>
            This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Pinto Injury Resources</strong> (“we,” “us,” or “our”) collects,
            uses, and shares information when you visit or interact with <strong>pintoinjury.com</strong> (the “Site”).
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
            <strong>Important:</strong> Pinto Injury Resources is an informational resource operated by a law student. It
            is <strong>not</strong> a law firm and does not provide legal advice or legal representation. Using this Site
            does not create an attorney–client relationship.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>Information we collect</h2>

          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Information you provide</h3>
<p style="margin-top: 0;">
  If you contact us by email, phone, or a form we may add in the future, you may provide information such as your name,
  email address, phone number, and a message describing your situation. This information is used solely to respond to
  your inquiry and provide general informational assistance.
</p>
<p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
  Email sent to addresses at this domain (for example, <em>info@pintoinjury.com</em>) may be forwarded to another email
  account using third-party email services. Messages may be accessible to individuals assisting with site operations
  or communications. Please do not include confidential, sensitive, or time-critical information.
</p>

          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>How we use information</h2>
          <p>We may use information we collect to:</p>
          <ul style="line-height: 1.7;">
            <li>operate, maintain, and improve the Site;</li>
            <li>respond to messages and inquiries;</li>
            <li>protect the Site, prevent abuse, and troubleshoot issues;</li>
            <li>understand which pages are helpful to visitors (for example, through aggregated usage trends).</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>How we share information</h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell your personal information. We may share information in limited situations, including:
          </p>
          <ul style="line-height: 1.7;">
            <li>
              <strong>Service providers:</strong> The Site is hosted and delivered using third-party services (for
              example, Cloudflare) that may process information to provide hosting, security, and performance.
            </li>
            <li>
  <strong>Email delivery and forwarding:</strong> Emails sent through this Site may be processed and forwarded by
  third-party email and infrastructure providers in order to deliver messages to us.
</li>

            <li>
              <strong>Legal and safety reasons:</strong> We may disclose information if required by law, or if necessary
              to protect the rights, safety, and security of visitors and the Site.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Attorney connections (when appropriate):</strong> If you ask to be connected with an independent,
              licensed California attorney, we may share only the information reasonably necessary to make that
              connection (for example, your name and contact information). No referral fees are accepted or paid.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
          <p>
            Our hosting and security providers may use cookies or similar technologies to deliver the Site, protect
            against abuse, and improve performance. If we add analytics tools in the future, we will update this policy
            to describe what is used and how to opt out where applicable.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
            You can control cookies through your browser settings. Note that disabling cookies may affect certain site
            features.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            We keep personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to respond to inquiries, maintain business
            records, and operate the Site, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law. We may also
            retain aggregated or de-identified information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>Your choices</h2>
          <ul style="line-height: 1.7;">
            <li>
              <strong>Opt out of communications:</strong> You can ask us to stop contacting you by replying to an email or
              contacting us using the information below.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Access / correction / deletion:</strong> You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of
              personal information you previously provided. We may need to verify your request and may retain certain
              information as required by law or for legitimate business purposes.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
          <p>
            This Site is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from
            children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information, please contact us and we will
            take appropriate steps.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>External links</h2>
          <p>
            The Site may contain links to third-party websites (for example, official resources or other informational
            sites). We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those third parties.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make changes, we will update the “Last updated”
            date above. Continued use of the Site after an update means you accept the revised policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or your information, you can contact us here:
          </p>
          <ul style="line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 0;">
            <li>
              Contact page: <a href="/contact">https://pintoinjury.com/contact</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              Email: <em>info@pintoinjury.com</em>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="surface" style="padding: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; opacity: 0.85;">
  <strong>Reminder:</strong> This Site provides general educational information only and does not provide legal advice.
  Contacting this Site, including by email, does not create an attorney–client relationship. Do not send confidential
  information unless and until an attorney–client relationship has been formally established with a licensed attorney.
</p>

        </section>
      </article>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
